SECTION 1 (Section 14-17-325): The clerk of court shall report to the State Law Enforcement Division, within forty-eight hours, the issuance of any: ... orders preventing a person from possessing a firearm;
SECTION 2 (new Section 22-1-200): Magistrates shall report to the State Law Enforcement Division, within forty-eight hours, the issuance of any: ... orders preventing a person from possessing a firearm;
SECTION 3 (new Section 14-25-250): A municipal judge shall report to the State Law Enforcement Division, within forty-eight hours, the issuance of any: ... orders preventing a person from possessing a firearm;
SECTION 4 (new Section 23-1-250): Each law enforcement agency must report to the State Law Enforcement Division within twenty-four hours: any incident in which a person may be prohibited from obtaining or possessing a firearm by state or federal law.
